    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0073" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">FW 841.51/8–1247</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Balfour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1947-08-14">August 14, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have received
                    your letter of August 12<anchor n="1" xml:id="d33-f1"/> advising me that your
                    government’s delegation for the forthcoming talks on financial matters will
                    arrive in Washington this weekend in anticipation of discussions beginning
                    Monday.</p>
                <pb facs="0074" n="56" xml:id="pg56"/>
                <p>On our side these discussions will be conducted by the National Advisory Council
                    on International Monetary and Financial Problems, of which, as you know, the
                    Secretary of Treasury is Chairman. I have informed Mr. Snyder of the contents of
                    your letter.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
